# Reverse proxy in front of the gateway container. Caddy handles automatic
# HTTPS (Let's Encrypt) so the gateway itself never needs a TLS cert.
#
# Replace the placeholder below with your real domain before first run, or
# use ":80" temporarily against a bare IP (no TLS) while DNS propagates.
#
# GATEWAY_PUBLIC_URL in .env must match this domain exactly (https://...),
# per CLAUDE.md Section 17 — the reference agent's outbound call to
# "the public URL" only proves anything if it is genuinely this domain,
# not the EC2 instance's private/loopback address.

your-domain.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4021
}
